        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(node-host): preserve JSON parse error cause in decodeParams",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `decodeParams` in `src/node-host/invoke.ts` discards the original `JSON.parse` error when `paramsJSON` is malformed. Users only see a generic \"paramsJSON malformed JSON\" message with no indication of what went wrong or where.\n\n**Solution**: Preserve the original error as `cause` and propagate it through the error result serialization and gateway protocol schema.\n\n**What changed** (3 files, 13 original lines → 52 after tests):\n- `invoke.ts`: capture parse error with `catch (err)` + `{ cause: err }`; propagate cause through sendErrorResult/sendInvalidRequestResult; add resolveErrorMessage helper to safely handle Error, string, and undefined cause types; update error types with optional cause field\n- `invoke.test.ts`: verify cause propagation through `handleInvoke` for both `system.run` and `system.run.prepare` commands\n- `nodes.ts` (gateway-protocol): add `cause: NonEmptyString` to NodeInvokeResultParamsSchema error object\n\n**What did NOT change**: Error code, message format, any other error paths, or any existing behavior. Fully backward compatible.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`decodeParams` used `catch {}` (no error variable) which discards the parse error. The JSON parse error with exact position information was permanently lost. Two layers lacked `cause` support: the serialization layer and the gateway protocol schema (`additionalProperties: false` on error object).\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Malformed paramsJSON error now includes parse error cause through the full `handleInvoke` → node.invoke.result pipeline.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Vitest executing the actual `handleInvoke` request handler (not mocked core logic).\n\n**After-fix test output** — exercises `handleInvoke` through real code paths:\n```\n$ npx vitest run src/node-host/invoke.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n ✓ wraps malformed paramsJSON for built-in commands\n ✓ wraps malformed paramsJSON for system.run.prepare command\n ✓ includes effective exec policy in system.run.prepare responses\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed | 3 skipped (6)\n```\n\nThe tests verify that `handleInvoke` → `decodeParams` → `sendInvalidRequestResult` produces error results with:\n```json\n{\n  \"code\": \"INVALID_REQUEST\",\n  \"message\": \"Error: INVALID_REQUEST: paramsJSON malformed JSON\",\n  \"cause\": \"Expected property name or } in JSON at position 1 (line 1 column 2)\"\n}\n```\n\n**What was not tested**: Remote node-host → gateway WebSocket round trip (requires full gateway deployment with connected node-host process).\n\n## Risk checklist\n\nmerge-risk: Low\n\n- [x] Low risk — 3 files, additive change only\n- [x] Backward compatible — errors without `cause` pass unchanged\n- [x] Strict schema preserved — unknown fields still rejected\n- [x] `resolveErrorMessage` safely handles Error, string, and undefined cause values\n- [x] No config or docs changes needed",
        "branch": "fix/node-host-preserve-json-parse-error-cause",
